Author: piggidragon <piggidragon.dev@proton.me>
Date:   Mon Aug 24 11:38:36 2026 +0200

    cuda: add opt-in host-KV transport telemetry
    
    Counts and times the blocking host-to-device deliveries performed by
    ggml_backend_cuda_buffer_set_tensor and the compute-stream drains
    performed by ggml_backend_cuda_synchronize. Opt-in through
    GGML_KV_TRANSPORT_STATS; no routing decision reads it and the counters
    are not touched when it is unset.
    
    Measured on RTX 4070 / Qwen3.8-27B-UD-IQ2_M, q8_0 K/V, -nkvo 1
    --kv-cpu-pinned, by differencing tg128 against tg64 at fixed depth so
    prefill and cache population cancel:
    
      depth 4,096:  31.6 t/s, 31.6 ms/token
                    6.31 ms/token blocking H2D, 151.8 MB/token (24.1 GB/s)
                    24.89 ms/token backend sync, 108 syncs/token
      depth 32,768: 12.98 t/s, 77.0 ms/token
                    47.02 ms/token blocking H2D, 1.150 GB/token (24.5 GB/s)
                    29.28 ms/token backend sync, 108 syncs/token
    
    The two terms account for 31.2 of 31.6 ms and 76.3 of 77.0 ms, so decode
    with host-resident KV is entirely host-thread blocking and the transfer
    is fully serialized against compute. Effective bandwidth is already at
    the practical PCIe 4.0 x16 ceiling, so the headroom is in overlap and in
    bytes moved, not in copy efficiency.
    
    Disabled-path no-op check, A/B/A at depth 4,096, r=5:
      base 31.79 +/- 0.12, telemetry build 31.73 +/- 0.11, base 31.70 +/- 0.13.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
